# Repository management

- Repository handlers coordinate persistence in `internal/database` with checkout operations in `internal/git` (native `git` via `os/exec`). There is no build step.
- Local checkouts live below `repositories/`; validate names and derived paths before filesystem or command operations.
- Git operations depend on host Git/LFS, SSH configuration, and credentials. Never expose stored authentication fields in responses or logs.
- Pull and branch start responses include `job_id`. Agents poll `GET /repo/job?job_id=` until the job is `success` or `error`; failure `detail` is the terminal error text.
- Persist a `repo_jobs` row as `running` before starting the goroutine. If the goroutine cannot start after insert, mark the job `error`.
- Those operations still update `repositories.status` (`idle`, `cloning`, `pulling`, `error`) asynchronously for UI labels; preserve terminal status on every exit path.
- Schema or status changes require checking the Repositories page, `docs/REPOSITORY_MANAGEMENT.md`, and `docs/API.md`.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/handlers/repo/... ./internal/database/...`.
